 ## Still open
+- **Bug: filled shapes in the Settings Menu ignore the palette and draw white** (reported in the editor). Rows, tabs (the selected tab too), buttons such as Reset, and slider / switch tracks stay pure white whatever `Row`, `RowHovered`, `RowFocused`, `Surface`, `Accent` or `Track` say; text colours, Accent on section headings, Background, Row Height and fonts all follow the style, so the style reaches the widget. Likely cause, found by reading: `MenuDraw::RoundedBox` / `RoundedBoxAt` (`Menu/Widgets/SMenuControls.cpp`) put the colour only in the `FSlateRoundedBoxBrush` and call `FSlateDrawElement::MakeBox` without a tint; `MakeBox` draws with its tint argument (default white) and does not apply the brush's own tint (`SImage` multiplies it in by hand), while every other `MakeBox` in the plugin passes its colour as the tint. Fix: pass `Fill` as the tint (brush fill white) and check the outline still takes its own colour. This is probably also why the Console preset's light text was unreadable (white rows under it). Repro: `create_settings_menu` {name SettingsMenu, tabs Controls / Video / Audio / Accessibility, style simple}, then set `Style.Colors.Row` = #1A1A1A on `DA_SettingsMenu_Style` (Preset Custom): `get_asset` reads the colour back, the rows in the `WBP_SettingsMenu` designer stay white (assets in `/NameTBD/NameTBD/AI/`). A designer preview cache is not yet ruled out: reopen the Blueprint or check in Play.
+- **Reported: `create_settings_menu` with style "simple" made a style asset with Preset = Console.** Not reproduced by reading: `StylePresetName` maps simple / dark / flat / empty to Simple and `ApplyPreset` sets it (`NameTBDAI/Private/NameTBDAITools_Menus.cpp`). Check the tool call's actual arguments in the chat log, and whether something later wrote the Preset (the `style_props` / `colors` path only sets Custom).
+- **A fully AAA, art-directed menu (Deadlock-style) cannot be built with the Settings Menu yet.** The Menu Style asset sets colours, fonts, sizes, corner radius, tab style, background image / blur, motion and sounds only; every part is drawn by the plugin's Slate code. Custom UMG rows are the only part that can be replaced, and they lose the panel's features (below). Today the closest route is Custom Rows plus a UMG screen around the Settings Menu (its tabs, search and footer hidden), or a fully hand-built screen of Menu Setting Row Widgets calling the subsystem. What it needs:
+  - Brushes / materials / SVGs (Image Source + SVG field, per-instance material inputs through `Widgets/WidgetEffectImage`) for every part and state: row background, focus bar, switch, slider track / thumb, selector chevrons, pips, segmented buttons, dropdown, tabs, footer prompts, description panel, dialogs, scroll bar.
+  - UMG classes for tabs, section and key-binding category headings, footer prompts, description panel, search box, dialogs, and each control (switch, slider, selector, segmented, dropdown, key slot, action button); standalone UMG controls (Menu Selector / Segmented / Slider / Switch) usable outside the Settings Menu.
+  - Custom Rows chosen per Choice Display (Selector / Buttons / Dropdown) and per setting or section, not only per kind.
+  - Custom rows inside the panel: `SMenuSettingsPanel::AddRow` returns before adding them to `Rows`, so focus restore after rebuilds, Focus First Setting, the description panel, narration, navigate / change sounds and footer actions on the focused row ignore them.
+  - Row state events on Menu Setting Row Widget (hover, focus, pressed, disabled, stepped left / right) to drive animations such as chevron bumps and segment slides, and access to the style's colours and fonts.
+  - `USettingsMenu::CustomRows` only grows: `BuildRows` clears the Slate children but the old row objects stay until `ReleaseSlateResources`.
+- Reuse or move an existing setting onto another page / section (an "Existing Setting" entry by Id); today a same-Id setting replaces it in place, so a copy with a new Id and the original in Hidden Settings is needed.
+- Per-menu Hidden Settings / sections (Hidden Pages / Settings are project-wide; a menu filters whole pages only).
+- Settings from a menu's Extra Schemas exist only while that menu is shown, so gameplay reads fail while it is closed: warn, validate, or offer registering for the game's lifetime.
+- Blueprint: build and register schemas at run time (setting fields are BlueprintReadOnly; no helper nodes); a Get Options event on Blueprint Target for dynamic choices (unlocked heroes, owned items).
+- Per-context settings (per hero / weapon): an inherit mode ("use common setting X") instead of an override Bool + Shown When + fallback code, and templated sections repeated per context.
+- Events: a "bind to setting and call now" node (On Setting Changed does not fire at start); telling preview from commit under the Apply Button policy (On Setting Changed fires for pending values and again on Revert).
+- Scale By Setting / Dead Zone By Setting read one fixed Id from the mapping context: a fallback Id and a per-pawn / per-context Id.
 - **Engine-built samples:** a shipped Content style asset, a sample settings Widget Blueprint and Key Glyph Sets with art (the code makes everything without assets; prompts show key caps until art is assigned).
 - CommonUI bridge (`NameTBDCommonUI`): Common Input type <-> Menu Input device, Common Action Widget glyphs, activatable widget stack for screens.
 - Audio output device selection (Audio Mixer `SwapAudioOutputDevice`), mono audio, dynamic range (night mode) - need audio mixer targets.
